  "f13df897-c073-4053-aa67-03d9968873e3"],
 " list them."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1b592f4e-a8f6-4c91-97b7-10f6efebed76"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraDeformation"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraDeformation", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b855152a-90b4-4491-883e-0c487b5522c3"],
 ", the complete vertex-list path must be simple, have the reference's \
ordered endpoints, stay inside its graph-distance tube, and satisfy the \
requested excess-length bounds. Membership is tested directly without \
constructing the counting graph. It does not certify a homotopy to the \
reference; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraDeformation"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraDeformation", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b9e64daa-c531-4d76-8528-0e151aedbf0e"],
 " searches for that additional certificate."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b51ab793-4f54-4a60-937c-fb3b4efb076a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraForwardDeformation"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraForwardDeformation", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d6c90177-6069-4a2e-a743-31b5693cdc1e"],
 ", the complete vertex-list walk must have the prescribed endpoints, stay in \
the reference tube, move forward through the distance shells, and satisfy the \
excess bound and first-arrival condition. The empty walk is not a member."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"84e9acde-6be2-46c5-87b7-1bfc43bf2b81"],

